                'School Of Agriculture And Natural Resources Management School Of Arts And Social Sciences School Of '
                'Business And Economics School Of Education And Human Resource Development School Of Health Sciences '
                'School Of Information Science & Technology School Of Law School Of Pure And Applied Sciences '
                'E-learning LIBRARY Website Myloft E-Resource Access Library Catalogue Institutional Repository '
                'RESEARCH Website Funding Opportunities External Research Grants Ongoing Research Projects COMPLIMENTS '
                '/ COMPLAINTS CONTACT US Search term Search Kisii University: Web People Search Web Other ways to '
                'search: Map Profiles Dr. Joseph Langat, PhD C.O.D, Agricultural Sciences Biography Profile: Dr. '
                'Joseph Kimutai Langat, PhD.; ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0587-8640 ; Email: '
                'drjosephlangat@kisiiuniversity.ac.ke & drjosephlangat@gmail.com ; Phone +254 722305965 Joseph Kimutai '
                'Langat, a duly registered member No. 777 of the Soil Science Society of East Africa (SSSEA) Kenya '
                'Chapter, is a senior lecturer of crop and soil sciences, Department of Agricultural Sciences, Kisii '
                'University, Kenya, and ILO-SIYB Certified Trainer in GYB-SYB-IYB ( '
                'https://webapps.ilo.org/siybgateway/Certification.action?id=128812 ). He serves as Adjunct Research '
                'Scientist at the African Institute for Capacity Development (AICAD), whose mandate is capacity '
                'building for poverty reduction in Africa by collaborating with the AICAD on applied research projects '
                'that address African development challenges such as sustainable development , co-authoring '
                'high-impact publications, building research networks, and contributing expertise and funding to '
                'jointly advance research, innovation, and knowledge transfer. Dr. Kimutai holds a PhD (crop '
                'ecophysiology from Moi University, MPhil (Moi), BSc & Diploma agronomy (both from Zhejiang '
                'University, China), postgraduate diploma in Mass Communication (KIMC, Nairobi) and a Diploma in '
                'Science Education. He served previously as a high school teacher (1989-2000), senior seed inspector '
                'KEPHIS (2000-2004), senior editor in charge of research and publishing- Jomo Kenyatta Foundation '
                '(2004-2015), Board of Management Chairperson of six schools at diverse dates (2010- date), Chief '
                'Officer Education Bomet County (2015-2017), and Dean- School of Agriculture at Lukenya University, '
                'Mtito Andei (2018-April 2019), University examination officer, and Campus Director in charge of Kisii '
                'University, Eldoret Campus (2022-2023). He is a CASSCOM member of Nyamira and Bomet County '
                '(2021-date), Editor-in-Chief of AJAUSUD Journal (2025- date), Chairman- Kisii University Agritech '
                '(2020-date), Chairman- Department of Education- Catholic Diocese of Kericho (2023-date), Chairman '
                'Bomet County Education Board (2024-date), Chairperson of the National Governing Council of the 47 '
                'County Education Board Chairpersons, among other accolades. He served as Editor-in-Chief (EiC) in the '
                '2 nd Kisii University International Multidisciplinary Conference (10-12 September 2024), whose theme '
                'was Strengthening African Economies Through Innovations for Sustainable Development , with 8 '
                'sub-themes and over 24 tracks. Peer reviewed and presented works were published in the Kisii '
                'University Book of Abstracts . Dr. Langat also serves as the EiC of the upcoming 3 rd Kisii '
                'University International Multidisciplinary Conference scheduled for 9 th to 11 th June 2026, whose '
                'theme is Reimagining Inclusive and Borderless Knowledge through Global Health for Sustainable '
                'Development . He has won numerous national and international scholarships and project grants, '
                'published widely in a number of high impact journals in his area of expertise (crop and soil). In '
                'December 2024, Joseph led a team of scientists as PI and won two 8-months project research grants '
                'worth Ksh. 500,000. He has supervised many undergraduate student projects and more than 10 MSc and '
                'PhD approved soil, crop and agricultural extension projects that lead to the award of the degrees of '
                'the University. One MSc student he supervised graduated in 2021, while three of them graduated in '
                '2025. He is trained and qualified in diverse fields: mass communication and journalism, report '
                'writing, senior management course (KSG), financial management, educational institutions management, '
                'winning grants project proposals writing, seed and plant varieties development, certification '
                'standards & processes. He is a consultant, a mentor to many, and conducts a number of humanitarian '
                'activities in the Kenyan villages. Research Interests No research interests provided. Education '
                'Background Litein High School 1980 - 1983 Division One Starehe Boys Centre & School Nairobi 1984 - '
                '1987 2P2S Moi Science Teachers College 1987 Sep - 1989 May Diploma Beijing Languages Institute, '
                'Peoples Republic of China 1990 Sep - 1991 June Diploma Zhejiang University, Hangzhou, Peoples '
                'Republic of China 1991 Sep - 1993 June Diploma Zhejiang University, Hangzhou, Zhejiang Province, '
                'Peoples Republic of China 1991 July - 1993 June Bachelors Moi University 1995 Sep - 2000 May Masters '
                'Kenya Institute of Mass Communication (KIMC) 2009 Sep - 2011 Oct Post Graduate Diploma Kenya School '
                'of Government 2013 May - 2013 June Certificate University of Eldoret 2005 Sep - 2014 May Doctor of '
                'Pholosophy(PhD) Start and Improve Your Business of the International Labour Organization (ILO-SIYB) '
                '2025 July - 2025 Dec Certificate Work Experience Kisii University June 2026 - Ongoing Catholic '
                'Diocese of Kericho, Kenya- Department of Education June 2023 - Ongoing International Labour '
                'Organisation Dec 2025 - Ongoing Ministry of Education, Department for Basic Education, Republic of '
                'Kenya March 2024 - Ongoing Ministry of Education, Department for Basic Education 2025 - Ongoing '
                'African Journal of Agriculture and Utilization of Natural Resources for Sustainable Development '
                '(AJAUSUD), Kisii University Jan 2026 - Ongoing African Institute for Capacity Development (AICAD) Nov '
                '2025 - Ongoing Publications No publications available. Research Grants Sustainable use of climate '
                'smart Zai pits for improved crop production in dry and nutrient Lelaitich ecosystem in Bomet County, '
                'Kenya PI: Joseph Kimutai Langat | Kisii University Board of Research & Innovation KES Enhancing soil '
                'properties and sustainable tomato yields through organic manure for climate change resilience and '
                'enhanced community livelihoods among smallholder farmers PI: Joseph Kimutai Langat | Kisii University '
                'Board of Research & Innovation KES Skills Soil & crop sciences expert Editing, , peer reviewing, page '
